{
  "overall_diagnosis": "Across samples, failures stem from quarter-scoping mismatches and broken/incomplete helper scripts. Multiple docs/examples don’t match the repo’s actual script locations and the dataset layout under /root/{quarter}/. Several scripts are syntactically truncated or contain malformed lists (missing commas), preventing execution. Even where runnable, key logic is wrong/underspecified: holding_analysis ignores the quarter argument and doesn’t output manager names; one_fund_analysis needs correct definitions for “number of stocks held” and a correct cross-quarter “Top Buys” calculation based on per-CUSIP VALUE deltas.",
  "diagnosed_skills": [
    {
      "path": "13f-analyzer/scripts/one_fund_analysis.py",
      "confidence": "high",
      "diagnosis": "Script appears syntactically broken (malformed title_class_of_stocks list due to missing commas; code truncated mid-statement) and likely miscomputes required metrics. It also needs correct quarter-scoped loading and correct cross-quarter Top Buys logic (VALUE deltas per CUSIP) plus an unambiguous “how many stocks held” metric.",
      "repair_instruction": "Make the file runnable end-to-end: (1) fix title_class_of_stocks list by adding missing commas between every string; (2) repair any truncated/incomplete lines (e.g., AUM print) and ensure imports/entrypoint work. (3) Ensure data loads from /root/{quarter}/INFOTABLE.tsv using the provided quarter argument. (4) In single-quarter mode, compute and print: total rows/positions; AUM = sum(VALUE) for the accession_number; and “number of stocks held” as count of distinct CUSIP after optional equity filtering via TITLEOFCLASS (keep both raw and filtered counts if needed). (5) In comparison mode, load both quarters, aggregate VALUE by CUSIP (sum), outer-join, fill missing with 0, compute delta = target - baseline; rank positive deltas descending as Top Buys (and optionally negative as Top Sells); output top-k with CUSIP and delta."
    },
    {
      "path": "13f-analyzer/scripts/holding_analysis.py",
      "confidence": "high",
      "diagnosis": "Quarter argument is ignored (reads /root/INFOTABLE.tsv instead of /root/{quarter}/INFOTABLE.tsv), which breaks quarter-specific answers. Output lacks fund manager names required by the task (prints only accession numbers).",
      "repair_instruction": "Use f\"{data_root}/{quarter}/INFOTABLE.tsv\" when reading holdings. After computing top-k ACCESSION_NUMBER by total VALUE for the given CUSIP, join with the quarter’s cover/manager metadata file (e.g., /root/{quarter}/COVERPAGE.tsv) on ACCESSION_NUMBER to retrieve FILINGMANAGER_NAME. Print ranked results including manager name, accession number, and total holding value."
    },
    {
      "path": "fuzzy-name-search/scripts/search_fund.py",
      "confidence": "high",
      "diagnosis": "Script is truncated/incomplete (ends at an unfinished function definition), making fuzzy/exact fund lookup unreliable or impossible; this blocks obtaining correct accession numbers per quarter.",
      "repair_instruction": "Complete and validate the script: load /root/{quarter}/COVERPAGE.tsv (or the correct coverpage filename) as strings; if --accession_number is provided, do exact match and return/print the single row with score=100; else run rapidfuzz.process.extract over FILINGMANAGER_NAME (optionally include other fields) using a stable scorer (e.g., fuzz.WRatio), print topk via pretty_print. Ensure main dispatch is correct and handles missing columns gracefully."
    },
    {
      "path": "fuzzy-name-search/scripts/search_stock_cusip.py",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "diagnosis": "Contains the same malformed title_class_of_stocks list (missing commas) and hardcodes reading 2025-q2 instead of taking a quarter parameter; excerpt suggests the matching logic may be incomplete (truncated at 'matches = process'). This affects locating a stock’s CUSIP (e.g., Palantir) for the required quarter.",
      "repair_instruction": "Fix title_class_of_stocks commas. Add a --quarter CLI argument and read /root/{quarter}/INFOTABLE.tsv. Complete fuzzy matching using rapidfuzz.process.extract (e.g., fuzz.WRatio) over NAMEOFISSUER, then print topk results with CUSIP, NAMEOFISSUER, TITLEOFCLASS. Ensure the script is syntactically complete and runnable as a CLI."
    },
    {
      "path": "13f-analyzer/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "diagnosis": "Documentation examples likely use inconsistent/incorrect invocation paths and do not clearly specify quarter-scoped data locations. It is also ambiguous about the correct definition of “how many stocks are held” and underspecifies cross-quarter Top Buys (should be ranked by per-CUSIP VALUE increase).",
      "repair_instruction": "Standardize all examples to repo-relative paths (e.g., python3 13f-analyzer/scripts/one_fund_analysis.py ...). Explicitly document the data layout under /root/{quarter}/ (INFOTABLE.tsv, COVERPAGE.tsv). Define metrics: total positions (rows) vs distinct CUSIPs (stocks held), and state which one answers the task. Document cross-quarter Top Buys precisely: aggregate by CUSIP, compute VALUE deltas (target-baseline), treat missing as 0, keep positive deltas, sort descending, and return top-k."
    }
  ],
  "unselected_skills": [
    "13f-analyzer/scripts/holding_analysis.py (additional doc updates beyond core fixes)",
    "fuzzy-name-search/SKILL.md"
